# alias: CompetitiveDoubles
# button-text: Competitive Doubles
# gib-works: true
# bba-works: true
# auction-filter: Auction.....\n1[HS] +X +Pass +(1S|2[CDH]) +2[HS]
# convention-card-ns: 21GF-DEFAULT
# convention-card-ew: 21GF-GIB

/*@chat
--- Competitive Doubles: the second takeout double
East opens 1!H or 1!S. You (South) make a takeout double, West passes, and
partner (North) advances as cheaply as he can in his best suit. East rebids
his suit. Your turn again.

"A double shows the values to compete in the bidding, but no clear opinion
about what to do." Your takeout double promised 3+ cards in every unbid
suit, so partner's suit may be the one you hold only three of — and a weak
partner had to bid SOMETHING. Choose by strength first, then by fit:

• Pass — a minimum takeout double (12-14 HCP). You have already described
  your hand; leave the rest to partner.
• Raise partner — extra values (17+ HCP, or 16 with a singleton) AND
  4+ card support for the suit partner bid.
• Double again — the same extra values but only 3-card support. The
  second takeout double says "I want to compete, but I do not know where."
  Partner can rebid his suit, try another suit, or pass for penalty with a
  trump stack. (With a strong 5-card minor of your own, bidding it at the
  3-level is the alternative; the robots often prefer it.)

A perfect second double: !SAK85 !H4 !DKT972 !CAJ6 after 1!H (X) P (2!C);
2!H (?) — extras, three clubs, and the diamonds are not worth 3!D on their own.

The robots (BBA and GIB) wait for about 17 before acting again; the article
is happier to compete on 14+. The 15-16 HCP hands where the styles part
company are left out of this scenario.

Level: intermediate.
Reference: https://www.advinbridge.com/this-week-in-bridge/647
@chat*/

dealer east

#include "script/TP"
# Provides tpWest, tpNorth, tpEast, tpSouth.

##### East opens 1H or 1S and later rebids it at the 2-level #####
# A 6-card major, at most a 4-card minor beside it, so the rebid is 2M
# rather than a second suit. 11-15 HCP: BBA opens 11 with a 6-card major;
# 16+ would jump to 3M.
oH = hearts(east)==6 and spades(east)<4
oS = spades(east)==6 and hearts(east)<4
eOneSuit = shape(east, any 6322 + any 6331 + any 6421)
eRange   = hcp(east)>10 and hcp(east)<16
eastHand = (oH or oS) and eOneSuit and eRange

##### South makes a takeout double (the student) #####
# Short in opener's major, 3+ in every unbid suit. Classic takeout shapes;
# any 5-card suit is a minor (a 5-card unbid major would overcall instead),
# and no 5332: with 3-3 beside the 5-card minor BBA overcalls the minor.
sShort = (oH and hearts(south)<3) or (oS and spades(south)<3)
sSupS  = oS or spades(south)>2
sSupH  = oH or hearts(south)>2
sSupport = sSupS and sSupH and diamonds(south)>2 and clubs(south)>2
sShape   = shape(south, any 4441 + any 4432 + any 5431 + any 5440 + any 5422)
sNoMajor5 = spades(south)<5 and hearts(south)<5

# Not a 1NT overcall: balanced 15-18 with a stopper (K or better) in their suit.
sStop = (oH and hcp(south,hearts)>2) or (oS and hcp(south,spades)>2)
sNT   = shape(south, any 4432 + any 5332) and hcp(south)>14 and sStop

# 12-18 HCP: strong enough to double, not strong enough to double and cuebid.
sRange    = hcp(south)>11 and hcp(south)<19 and tpSouth>11
southHand = sShort and sSupport and sShape and sNoMajor5 and sRange and not sNT

##### West passes #####
# Under 8 HCP so the robot has no 1NT and no redouble; fewer than 3 trumps so
# no raise; no 5-card suit to introduce, and over 1H a 4-card spade suit only
# with 0-4 HCP (BBA bids 1S on it from 5).
wWeak    = hcp(west)<8
wNoRaise = (oH and hearts(west)<3) or (oS and spades(west)<3)
wNoLong  = spades(west)<5 and hearts(west)<5 and diamonds(west)<5 and clubs(west)<5
wNo1S    = oS or spades(west)<4 or hcp(west)<5
westHand = wWeak and wNoRaise and wNoLong and wNo1S

##### North advances as cheaply as he can in his longest unbid suit #####
# 0-7 HCP: with 8 BBA advances 1NT (stopper or not) or jumps on a 5-card
# suit. Over 1H a 4+ card spade suit is bid at the 1-level (1S) with 0-6
# HCP (BBA jumps to 2S with 7), the rest at the 2-level. The bid suit is the UNIQUE longest unbid suit of 4 or 5
# cards (a 6-card suit jumps), so we know which suit South must support —
# except 4-4 in the minors when South holds the minors equally, where
# either bid lands in the same band. No 5-card stack in opener's suit
# (that is a penalty pass).
nS = oS ? 0 : spades(north)
nH = oH ? 0 : hearts(north)
nD = diamonds(north)
nC = clubs(north)

nBidS = oH and nS>3 and nS<6 and nS>=nD and nS>=nC and hcp(north)<7
nBidH = oS and nH>3 and nH<6 and nH>nD and nH>nC
nBidD = nD>3 and nD<6 and nD>nH and nD>nC and nD>nS
nBidC = nC>3 and nC<6 and nC>nH and nC>nD and nC>nS
nBidDC = nD>3 and nD<6 and nD==nC and nD>nH and nD>nS and diamonds(south)==clubs(south)
nBids = nBidS or nBidH or nBidD or nBidC or nBidDC

nNoStack  = (oH and hearts(north)<5) or (oS and spades(north)<5)
nRange    = hcp(north)<8
northHand = nBids and nNoStack and nRange

##### South's second decision: the three hand types #####
# Support for the suit North bid (a 4-4 minor tie falls through to clubs,
# which South then holds equally with diamonds).
sFit = nBidS ? spades(south) : (nBidH ? hearts(south) : (nBidD ? diamonds(south) : clubs(south)))

# Minimum = 12-14 HCP; extras = 18+ total points (17 HCP, or 16 with a
# singleton). The 15-17 HCP hands in between are where styles differ (the
# article acts on about 14+; BBA and the robots wait for 17), so leave them out.
sMin   = hcp(south)<15
sExtra = tpSouth>17
# 3-card support with extras is nearly always a 5431 with a 5-card minor
# (a 4441 short in their suit is 4-4-4 in the unbid suits). BBA bids that
# minor at the 3-level about a third of the time; the article doubles.
sPass  = sMin
sRaise = sExtra and sFit>3
sX     = sExtra and sFit==3

HandType_Pass  = sPass
HandType_Raise = sRaise
HandType_X     = sX

### BEGIN GENERATED LEVELING ###
noLeveling = 1
levelTheDeal = noLeveling
### END GENERATED LEVELING ###

##### Now do it #####
eastHand and southHand and westHand and northHand and (sPass or sRaise or sX) and levelTheDeal

action
average "E 1H            " 100 * oH,
average "E 1S            " 100 * oS,
average "N bids 1S       " 100 * nBidS,
average "N bids 2H       " 100 * nBidH,
average "N bids 2D       " 100 * nBidD,
average "N bids 2C       " 100 * nBidC,
average "S pass  (12-14) " 100 * sPass,
average "S raise (18+,4)" 100 * sRaise,
average "S X     (18+,3)" 100 * sX,
average "E HCP avg       "       hcp(east),
average "S HCP avg       "       hcp(south),
average "S TP  avg       "       tpSouth,
average "N HCP avg       "       hcp(north),
average "W HCP avg       "       hcp(west),
